.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt TCX 4 aarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tcx
.Nd "Toshiba TC956x PCIe 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet driver"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device pci"
.Cd "device iflib"
.Cd "device tcx"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if_tcx_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Ethernet ports of the Toshiba TC956x,
a PCI Express switch with an internal endpoint whose two PCI functions
each contain a Synopsys XGMAC Ethernet controller,
an XPCS and a SerDes.
Each function appears as a separate
.Nm
interface.
.Pp
The driver restarts each controller from reset when it attaches,
and follows the PHY as its link changes speed:
the PHY carries 2.5 Gbit/s over 2500BASE-X
and lower speeds over SGMII,
and the driver switches the SerDes and XPCS to match.
The PHY is polled for link state.
.Pp
Flow control is negotiated by the PHY.
When the link partner agrees, the controller sends PAUSE frames as its
receive FIFO fills and obeys PAUSE frames it receives;
the negotiated result appears as
.Cm rxpause
and
.Cm txpause
in the media status reported by
.Xr ifconfig 8 .
.Pp
The driver supports transmit and receive checksum offload for TCP and UDP
over IPv4 and IPv6, and for the IPv4 header,
controlled with the
.Cm txcsum ,
.Cm rxcsum ,
.Cm txcsum6
and
.Cm rxcsum6
options of
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
and TCP segmentation offload over IPv4 and IPv6,
controlled with the
.Cm tso4
and
.Cm tso6
options.
.Pp
Jumbo frames are supported, up to an MTU of 9000 bytes.
.Pp
Interrupts are moderated.
Received frames raise an interrupt through a watchdog timer that runs
from the first frame not yet reported,
rather than one interrupt per frame,
and transmit completions are reported at most once per
.Va tx_coal_frames
descriptors;
see
.Sx SYSCTL VARIABLES .
.Pp
The
.Nm
driver supports the following media types:
.Bl -tag -width ".Cm 10baseT/UTP"
.It Cm autoselect
Enables auto-negotiation for speed and duplex.
.It Cm 10baseT/UTP
Sets 10 Mbit/s operation.
.It Cm 100baseTX
Sets 100 Mbit/s operation.
.It Cm 1000baseT
Sets 1000 Mbit/s operation.
.It Cm 2500baseT
Sets 2500 Mbit/s operation.
.El
.Pp
Selecting a fixed media type limits what the PHY advertises to that
speed; the link is still auto-negotiated.
Only
.Cm full-duplex
operation is supported.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the Ethernet functions of the following controllers:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Toshiba TC9564 (also sold as the Qualcomm QPS615)
.El
.Pp
It has been tested on the Radxa Dragon Q8B, whose two 2.5 Gbit/s ports
are TC9564 functions, each wired to a Qualcomm QCA8081 PHY.
.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
Tunables can be set at the
.Xr loader 8
prompt before booting the kernel or stored in
.Xr loader.conf 5 .
The
.Va rx_riwt ,
.Va rx_coal_frames
and
.Va tx_coal_frames
variables described in
.Sx SYSCTL VARIABLES
can also be set as tunables, for example
.Va dev.tcx.1.rx_riwt .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va hw.tcx.cold_init
When set to 1, the default, each controller, SerDes and XPCS is
restarted from reset when the driver attaches.
When set to 0, a controller that firmware left running is kept as it is,
which avoids dropping the link, for example when the system was booted
from the network.
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following variables are available for each interface as
.Va dev.tcx.\& Ns Ar N :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va rx_riwt
The receive interrupt watchdog, in units of 256 DMA clock cycles,
about 2 microseconds.
An interrupt is raised this long after the first received frame that
has not been reported yet.
Larger values mean fewer interrupts and more latency.
The default is 64, about 130 microseconds;
0 raises an interrupt for every frame.
.It Va rx_coal_frames
When
.Va rx_riwt
is set, also raise an interrupt for every this many received frames.
The default, 0, relies on the watchdog alone.
.It Va tx_coal_frames
Report transmit completions at most once per this many descriptors.
The default is 128.
.It Va rx_errors
Frames received with an error, such as a bad checksum.
They are passed up without checksum offload flags,
so the network stack checks them itself.
.It Va rx_error_status
The receive descriptor status of the last such frame.
.It Va intr , intr_rx , intr_tx
The number of interrupts taken, and of those that reported received
frames or transmit completions.
.It Va mmc_rx_frames
Frames received by the MAC, good and bad.
.It Va mmc_rx_crc_errors
Frames received with a CRC error.
.It Va mmc_rx_fifo_overflow
Frames dropped because the receive FIFO was full.
.It Va mmc_rx_discard
Frames discarded by the MAC.
.It Va mtl_rxq0_missed
The raw missed and overflow packet counts of receive queue 0.
.It Va rx_buf_unavail
The number of times the receive DMA found no free descriptor.
.It Va dma_bus_errors
The number of fatal DMA bus errors.
.It Va serdes
The state of the SerDes and XPCS, for debugging.
.It Va serdes_reset
Writing 1 makes the driver set up the SerDes and XPCS again at the next
link check.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "tcx%d: function 0 has not set up the chip"
Function 1 attached before function 0,
which must set up the parts of the chip that both functions share.
.It "tcx%d: cannot allocate an MSI"
The driver needs one MSI per function.
.It "tcx%d: MAC %d did not start cleanly"
Restarting the controller, SerDes or XPCS from reset timed out;
the driver attaches anyway and tries again at the next link check
that finds the PHY up.
.It "tcx%d: PHY at %d does not answer"
No PHY responded on the controller's MDIO bus.
.It "tcx%d: SerDes did not come up at %u Mb/s"
The SerDes did not finish initializing for the new link speed.
.It "tcx%d: PCS reset timed out"
The XPCS did not come out of reset.
.It "tcx%d: DMA reset timed out"
The controller's DMA did not finish its software reset;
the interface stays down.
.It "tcx%d: DMA bus error, status 0x%08x"
The controller reported a fatal error while accessing host memory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr altq 4 ,
.Xr iflib 4 ,
.Xr netintro 4 ,
.Xr ng_ether 4 ,
