.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
device driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
driver and this manual page were written by
.An James Kane .
.Sh CAVEATS
There is no public documentation for the TC956x.
.Pp
The driver expects the PHY at MDIO address 28 and reads its link state
from a Qualcomm QCA808x status register, as on the Radxa Dragon Q8B.
.Pp
The station address is kept in an I2C EEPROM that the driver cannot read.
The driver keeps the address firmware programmed into the controller;
if there is none, it generates one with
.Xr ether_gen_addr 9 .
.Sh BUGS
Multiple queues and Wake on LAN are not supported.
The MAC has no receive-side scaling hash, so more receive queues would
not spread traffic.
